  "id": "COMPOUND:16506 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a consistent relationship between the compound in question and SCCH-26, as it is all directed toward the same target: Dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase. This kinase is a target of multiple compounds, including 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine, Javanicoside F, and Corticatic Acid E, all of which have been shown to interact with SCCH-26. The shared target indicates a potential mechanism of action where the compound in question may exert its effects through a common pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of this kinase. The evidence is robust and consistent across different compounds, suggesting a possible role in the regulation of cellular processes through this kinase. The integration of these findings highlights the importance of this kinase as a potential mediator in the biological effects of the compound, though further studies are needed to elucidate the exact mechanism of interaction.",
